# Agentic / implementation routing

**ADF status mirror: COMPLETE ADF-A–ADF-H; ADF-EX-17 DEFERRED VERIFICATION; FOUNDATION EXIT ACCEPTED; IMPLEMENTATION 001-A NEXT.**

**CKR status mirror: COMPLETE CKR-A–CKR-J; NEXT CKR-K; IMPLEMENTATION 001-A BLOCKED ON CKR EXIT.**

CKR-A–J are complete/accepted. CKR-K is next/ready but unstarted. Product implementation remains blocked until CKR-K.

Primary shared authority remains root `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agentic_development_foundation/authority_scope_policy.md`, the CKR README/ownership inventory, and accepted ADF scope/security mechanics. All accepted semantic families through ARCH are canonicalized; Phase 001–010 sources are provenance.

For a known stable ID, use `python3 scripts/agentic/resolve_stable_id.py <ID>` to get the deterministic canonical locator. Use `--history` only for explicit provenance/history. For an unknown semantic location, use one bounded route from `knowledge/index.md`, then the canonical owner.

Do not infer authority from OKF, resolver output alone, recency, search order, Git history, vendor skill, tool memory, source availability or path presence. CKR-J completion does not authorize CKR-K or implementation work.
